            <ArticleTitle>[Spirometry parameters of women in various positions of delivery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>911-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">Position in labour depends mostly on women's preferences, and is chosen instinctively in order to reduce labour pain. Between two different positions: vertical and horizontal, the first of them seems to guarantee more convenient gas exchange in maternal lungs.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">To prove that the vertical position in labour increase spirometry parameters in comparison with horizontal one.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Women were divided into two groups according to position in labour and spirometry examination were performed in second period of labour. Group I were composed of 17 women in vertical position whereas group II--19 women in horizontal one.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Whole of analysed spirometral parameters had higher values in group I (8.2%-17.1%), but the increase wasn't statistically significant (p &lt; 0.05).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
